hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18011","Al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, Abdullah said: And I heard it myself from al-Hakam: Shihab ibn Khirash narrated to us, Shuayb ibn Ruzayq al-Taifi narrated to me, he said: I was sitting with a man called al-Hakam ibn Hazn al-Kulafi, and he had companionship from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Then he began narrating to us, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as the seventh of seven or the ninth of nine, he said: Then he gave us permission and we entered, and we said: O Messenger of Allah, we came to you that you supplicate for us for good, he said: Then he supplicated for us for good and ordered concerning us, so we were lodged, and he ordered for us something of dates, and the condition at that time was meagre, he said: Then we stayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) days in which we witnessed Friday, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood leaning upon a bow, or he said upon a staff, then he praised Allah and extolled Him with light, good, blessed words, then he said: O people, you will not do and you will not be able to do all that you are commanded, but be straight and rejoice."
"18012","Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, Shihab ibn Khirash ibn Hawshab narrated to us, Shuayb ibn Ruzayq al-Taifi narrated to us, he said: I sat with a man who had companionship from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called al-Hakam ibn Hazn al-Kulafi, then he began narrating, and he mentioned its meaning."
